@page "/docs/cli/changes"

@* --dry-run, --diff and --json; what izzy does with files you've changed; exit codes (Cli.cs). *@

<ArticlePage Section="cli" Slug="changes">
    <Lead>
        You can see any change <Code>izzy</Code> would make before it makes it, as a list, a diff, or JSON for agents and
        scripts. izzy never replaces a file you've changed unless you ask it to.
    </Lead>
    <ChildContent>
        <Heading Level="2">See the changes first</Heading>
        <TextBlock>Add one of these options to any <Code>izzy add</Code> or <Code>izzy init</Code> command:</TextBlock>
        <Table Items="Previews" Caption="Showing changes" Size="ControlSize.Sm" Class="site-params" Bordered="false">
            <Columns>
                <TemplateColumn Title="Option" Width="Length.Rem(14)"><code>@context!.Name</code></TemplateColumn>
                <TemplateColumn Title="What it does">@context!.Text</TemplateColumn>
            </Columns>
        </Table>

        <Heading Level="2">JSON for agents and scripts</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            <Code>--json</Code> prints the changes as data: the files to create, the text to insert, the packages to add,
            any warnings, and any files that clash. Each insert includes its position and a hash of the file it was
            planned against.
        </TextBlock>
        <TextBlock>
            A coding agent can run the command with <Code>--dry-run --json</Code>, show you the changes, and then run it
            again without <Code>--dry-run</Code> once you agree.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Files you've changed</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            If a file izzy would create already exists with different content, izzy stops, writes nothing and tells you
            which file it is. To compare the two, run the command with <Code>--diff</Code>. To replace the file, run it with
            <Code>--overwrite</Code>.
        </TextBlock>
        <TextBlock>
            When izzy adds a line to one of your files, such as a <Code>@@using</Code>, it skips the line if it's already
            there.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Exit codes</Heading>
        <Table Items="ExitCodes" Caption="Exit codes" Size="ControlSize.Sm" Class="site-params" Bordered="false">
            <Columns>
                <TemplateColumn Title="Code" Width="Length.Rem(14)"><code>@context!.Name</code></TemplateColumn>
                <TemplateColumn Title="Meaning">@context!.Text</TemplateColumn>
            </Columns>
        </Table>

        <Heading Level="2">Next steps</Heading>
        <List Gap="2">
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/get-started/ai-assistants">AI assistants</Anchor>: connect your coding agent to IzzyBlazor's docs.</ListItem>
        </List>
    </ChildContent>
</ArticlePage>

@code {
    private sealed record Row(string Name, string Text);

    private static readonly Row[] Previews =
    [
        new("--dry-run", "Lists what would change, and writes nothing."),
        new("--diff", "Shows the changes as a unified diff."),
        new("--json", "Prints the changes as JSON. izzy list and izzy describe take it too."),
    ];

    private static readonly Row[] ExitCodes =
    [
        new("0", "Done, or there was nothing to change."),
        new("1", "An error, such as an unknown setting, or an app that doesn't build after izzy init."),
        new("2", "A file already exists with different content. Nothing was written."),
        new("3", "The item or layout needs IzzyBlazor Pro. izzy list marks these items."),
    ];
}
